        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0638" n="526" xml:id="pg526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123J634/359: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-20T17:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>254. The appointed Chinese Ambassador is to present his letters of credence to
                    the President on August 21.</p>
                <p>Due to the fact that the President expects to leave Washington in the near future
                    and the date of his return is uncertain, it has seemed impracticable to endeavor
                    to arrange that the Chinese Ambassador present his letters of credence on
                    approximately the date set for you to present your letters of credence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
